Lingo word decks
Copyright (c) 2026 Riley Busche

The word decks (data/*/deck.ts) and the data files they are built from (in the
development repository: scripts/build-deck/<lang>/*.json and
scripts/build-deck/<lang>/*/*.json) are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
licence (CC BY-SA 4.0):

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

You may share and adapt them, for any purpose, as long as you credit the
sources below, link to the licence, say what you changed, and release your
version under the same licence.

They are adapted from:

  FrequencyWords by Hermit Dave
  https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords
  (content licensed CC BY-SA 4.0; commit 525f9b5, content/2018/<list>/<list>_50k.txt,
  the list for each language: es, fr, it, and pt_br for Portuguese)

  which is counted from the OpenSubtitles 2018 corpus, http://www.opensubtitles.org/
  P. Lison and J. Tiedemann, 2016, "OpenSubtitles2016: Extracting Large Parallel
  Corpora from Movie and TV Subtitles", in Proceedings of the 10th International
  Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC 2016).

Changes: word forms grouped into dictionary words, re-ranked by their summed
counts and cut to the top 1,000; English meanings, part of speech, gender,
article and one example sentence per word added. The sentences were written fresh; no
subtitle text is included.

The build scripts and prompts (in the development repository: scripts/build-deck/*.ts,
scripts/build-deck/prompts/) are code, under the MIT licence in LICENSE.
